e, libretto of Così fan tutte (1790)","author":"Lorenzo Da Ponte (1749–1838)","licence":"Public domain","notes":"Words as printed in the Peters vocal score (Non v'e without the accent, Muojo)."},{"item":"Score (score.musicxml)","source":"Edition Peters vocal score (Edition Peters Nr. 4474, plate 11446, edited by Georg Schünemann), pages 55–56, the recitative between No. 8 and No. 9 (12 bars)","author":"Kurt Soldan (1891–1946), piano reduction","licence":"Public domain","notes":"Written out from the printed pages: sung lines and piano each read by two independent readers, every disagreement settled on the page by a judge, then checked bar by bar by a fresh checker (one error found in bar 8 and corrected). Where the print gives a second rhythm for the German words, the Italian rhythm is kept. The German singing translation is left out. The sisters' last line, Muojo d'affanno, ends in the first bar of No. 9 (-fanno), which is not part of this piece. Playback tempo ♩ = 103, a nominal speaking pace for secco recitative, from Böhm's recording (0:28); Mozart gives no tempo."},{"item":"IPA, gloss and translation","source":"Written for this app (from the app's reviewed Così libretto drafts)","author":"Counterpart development team","licence":"CC0 1.0","notes":"Unreviewed by a diction coach."}],"files":{"musicxml":"score.musicxml","language":"language.json"},"importedAt":"2026-11-13T13:12:45.100Z"}